From: Andrew S Hall <ashall@magnus.acs.ohio-state.edu>
Subject: DIET: Vegan Book

I am not Vegan, but I do love to cook and cook a large variety of things.
I have two pieces of advice to someone who wants to adopt a vegan diet
and still enjoy really good food.

1) Buy a wok. Stir-frying vegtables is really easy and produces great food.
   Don't buy an electric wok. Buy a rolled steel one. The principle of
   a wok is a really, really hot spot in the center. An electric one just
   doesn't provide it as well.

2) The best cookbook I have found it _Laurel's Kitchen_. It also has a
   large section on nutrition. The newer edition may be OK in that
   section, but one should still be careful. Get independent confirmation
   of anything in it before accepting it. The recipes, however, are top
   notch.

3) Expect some problems when you first convert. Your intestines may rebel
   a first and many people often end up w/ large amounts of painful gas.
   This doesn't mean stop the diet or that a vegan diet is not for you,
   it just means you may have to plan a little more carefully.

4) Try the ADM Harvest Burgers. They are not a taste analogue for beef, but
   are really good on their own. Instead of reconstituing them with water,
   use a blend of water and your favorite BBQ sauce or other such sauces.
   It is amazing how delicious this is.

A.




